-- Owner-approved synthetic data correction (second of 2026-10-15): in the 11 corrected red-flag
-- lists, the GI-bleeding item moves from the "within a day" group to the end of the emergency group
-- (haematemesis and melaena on antiplatelets are emergencies). One transaction; the reviewed-record
-- guard on discharges is off only for these statements. Each update matches the seeded row AND
-- its exact previous list, and the DO block refuses to commit unless every count is as expected.
begin;
alter table public.discharges disable trigger guard_reviewed_child;
update public.discharges d set red_flags = array['Go to the nearest hospital emergency department or call 108 immediately if you have:', 'Chest pain or pressure lasting more than a few minutes, or coming back', 'Severe breathlessness', 'Fainting or collapse', 'Bleeding from the wrist puncture site that does not stop after 10 minutes of firm pressure', 'A rapidly growing swelling at the puncture site', 'The hand on that side becoming cold, pale, numb or very painful', 'Black or bloody stools, or vomiting blood (you are on blood-thinning tablets)', 'Contact the cardiology team within a day for:', 'Increasing pain, redness, warmth or discharge at the puncture site', 'Fever']::text[]
